        "name": "placeholder-invalid-after-extension",
        "description": "A placeholder (`#`) follows a user extension term (Item/Blech/#) or stands in for one (Item/#). The # cannot be an extension, so this is PLACEHOLDER_INVALID in every context, events file or sidecar. A validator that checks extensionAllowed or the term itself first may report TAG_EXTENSION_INVALID instead.",
        "warning": false,
        "schema": "8.5.0",
        "error_category": "semantic",
        "common_causes": [
            "Extending a tag with a new term and then putting the value column's # after the new term",
            "Putting # on a tag such as Item that allows extensions but does not take a value",
            "Assuming that a tag which can be extended can also take a value"
        ],
        "explanation": "A # placeholder may only replace the value of a tag whose schema node has a # child (Label/#, Age/#). A user extension such as Item/Blech is a new term, not a schema node, so it has no # child and cannot take a value; neither can a tag like Item, which allows extensions but takes no value. Use a tag that takes a value for the column's values, next to the extension if the term is needed.",
        "correction_strategy": "Move the # to a tag that takes a value, keeping any extension term as an ordinary tag",
        "correction_examples": [
            {
                "wrong": "trial: Item/Blech/#",
                "correct": "trial: Item/Blech, Label/#",
                "explanation": "The extension stays a tag; the column's value goes on Label, which takes a value"
            },
            {
                "wrong": "trial: Item/#",
                "correct": "trial: Item, Parameter-value/#",
                "explanation": "Item takes no value; Parameter-value does"
            }
        ],
        "specification_reference": "3.2.5. Tag extensions (rule 5); Appendix B PLACEHOLDER_INVALID d",
        "related_errors": [
            "PLACEHOLDER_INVALID",
            "TAG_EXTENSION_INVALID",
            "TAG_EXTENDED"
        ],
