            "Assuming that adding units makes the # a value"
        ],
        "explanation": "A # placeholder, with or without units, may only replace the value of a tag whose schema node has a # child (Weight/#, Duration/#). A user extension such as Item/Blech is a new term, not a schema node, so it has no # child and takes no value, and neither does a tag like Item. Units only say how to read a value; they cannot make a tag take one. Put the # and its units on a tag that takes a value of that kind, next to the extension if the term is needed.",
